From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/27] Answer memory requirements from earlier identical
 objects

Image and buffer memory requirements, including the dedicated-allocation
answer, are cached by the exact creation parameters on each device
(caboose-bounded-memory/requirements_cache.h), so an object made like an
earlier one learns them without a round trip. Objects with external memory,
DRM modifiers, swapchain or unknown extension structures are not cached.
---
 .../guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp      | 87 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.h        |  2 +
 2 files changed, 85 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
index e547d91..7867c9a 100644
